.TH GROOV 1 "2026-10-24" "groov 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
groov \- portable, extensible terminal music player
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B groov
[COMMAND] [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
groov is a local keyboard-driven terminal music player. It stores songs in an XDG-compatible directory library, delegates audio to an external player, and supports language-independent modules.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B tui
Open the player. This is the default command.
.TP
.B init
Create configuration and data directories.
.TP
.B uninstall
Permanently remove groov configuration, cache, modules, themes, and the local library after an explicit y/yes confirmation. The executable is not removed.
.TP
.B add FILE
Import an audio file. Use --copy, --dry-run, --id, --title, --artist, --album, --desc, --tag, --image, and --lyrics.
.TP
.B edit ID
Update existing song metadata.
.TP
.B list
List songs. Use --tag and --json.
.TP
.B scan
Validate the local library.
.TP
.B modules [list|install|remove|enable|disable|info]
Install and manage modules. The singular \fBmodule\fR alias is also accepted.
.TP
.B theme [list|install|use]
List, install, and activate themes.
.TP
.B doctor
Print paths, player, library, module, theme, repeat, and image diagnostics.
.TP
.B version
Print the current groov version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/groov/settings.json
Configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/groov/songs
Local song library.
.TP
.I ~/.config/groov/modules
Module manifests.
.TP
.I ~/.config/groov/themes
Theme files.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
XDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_DATA_HOME, and XDG_CACHE_HOME override the default directories. Modules receive GROOV_API_VERSION, GROOV_EVENT, GROOV_EVENT_JSON, GROOV_SONG_ID, GROOV_SONG_FILE, GROOV_CONFIG_DIR, GROOV_SETTINGS_FILE, GROOV_DATA_DIR, GROOV_SONGS_DIR, and GROOV_CACHE_DIR.
.SH SEE ALSO
The installed documentation and https://github.com/bluetoothpaste1/groov
